flickos-classroom-view (1.0~test3) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Phase 2: View and Control one student's screen through wayvnc on a
    Unix socket, piped through the agent's own TLS connection (ADR-012),
    with a strip at the top of the student's screen and its Stop (ADR-
    015; on a lab computer only for control, Q10); Show My Screen, the
    teacher's screen in the students' class lock (ADR-014), at most 2
    frames a second, 1280 wide while the network is slow (Q13). Depends
    on wayvnc, FlickOS's libneatvnc0 without H.264, gtk-vnc and gtk-
    layer-shell.
  * The screen window opens at 1280x680 (HIG WIN-3) and, when the screen
    can't be shown, the message fills it instead of an empty black
    display.
  * A view or control session counts as ended only once wayvnc and the
    strip are stopped and their files removed, so a new one started at
    that moment keeps its socket.

 -- Jon <dvbondoy@gmail.com>  Tue, 17 Nov 2026 23:18:21 +0800

